From a3b3c0f5fad6ee8b9968a99220b1bffed98587e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:36:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B4: read-only introspection tool (eo/introspection.py)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New backend/eo/introspection.py: list_directory(path), read_file(path),
  search_text(pattern, root) -- plain Python (os.listdir/os.walk,
  open(), re.search), no subprocess/shell. Every function calls
  eo/redaction_guard.py::is_readable() (Patch B2) before returning any
  content, directory entry, or search hit. A denied top-level path/root
  comes back as {"readable": False, ...} with no further detail --
  never an exception, never a distinguishable "exists but denied" vs.
  "doesn't exist" message, since either would let a rejection leak
  information about what's being hidden.
  - list_directory(): non-recursive; each entry carries its OWN
    readable flag (a listable directory doesn't make every file inside
    it readable) -- entry *names* are still shown even when denied,
    since existence isn't the thing being protected, content is.
  - read_file(): full text up to MAX_READ_BYTES (200_000, truncates
    rather than errors); binary/non-UTF-8 content comes back as
    error="not_text" rather than raw bytes or a decode exception.
  - search_text(): os.walk()'s `root` gates the whole call; each file
    encountered during the walk is independently checked too, and a
    denied file is silently skipped (not reported as an error or a
    count), since a growing "skipped: n" number would itself leak how
    much redacted content exists under a root. Capped at
    MAX_SEARCH_MATCHES (200, truncated=True when hit), each line
    previewed to 200 chars.
- backend/eo/capabilities.py: list_directory()/read_file()/search_text()
  registered as pass-throughs alongside the B0/B1/B3 functions, per
  this module's own docstring ("discoverable through the same shared
  surface... the fallback path when the capability layer doesn't
  precisely cover what an agent needs to know"). No call-order
  enforcement here -- that's Patch B5b, once B5a's agent wiring exists
  to enforce it against.
- Test: backend/tests/unit/test_eo_introspection.py -- reuses
  test_eo_redaction_guard.py's own _path_in() helper and its exact
  secret-pattern fixture cases (same boundary, not re-derived), plus
  real-repo-tree reads/lists/searches, per-entry/per-file redaction
  inside an otherwise-allowed root, not-a-file/not-a-directory/
  invalid-pattern operational errors, and the two caps
  (MAX_READ_BYTES truncation, MAX_SEARCH_MATCHES truncation).
- Full backend unit suite re-run after this patch: 3474 passed, 7
  skipped, 2 xfailed, 0 failed (+25 over the B3 baseline, all new).

Ref: MiniMe-CLI-Internal-Architecture-Plan.md §3.3
Ref: MiniMe-Patch-Series-B-Plan.md, Patch B4
Depends on: Patch B2 (eo/redaction_guard.py::is_readable() must exist -- this patch is its primary caller)
